! ADJUST_CORRECTIONS - Runtime correction scaling for CMFGEN
!
! Optional control file containing parameters that can be used to
! scale corrections in order to facilitate convergence.
! This file may be changed while the program is running.
! Used by $cmfdist/subs/fiddle_pop_corrections_v2.f
!
! NOTE: The scaled corrections are NOT applied to Lambda iterations.
!       This file only affects BA (full) iterations.
!
! Parameters:
!   [L_ST]       Beginning depth (default: 1 = outermost)
!   [L_END]      End depth (default: ND = innermost)
!   [RELAX]      Relaxation parameter (0 < Z < 2)
!                Z < 1: under-relaxation (damp oscillations)
!                Z = 1: normal (no scaling)
!                Z > 1: over-relaxation (faster convergence, risk divergence)
!   [T_LIM]      Maximum fractional change to temperature (0 < Z < 0.2)
!   [MAX_CHNG]   1 + maximum fractional increase for populations (> 1)
!                e.g. MAX_CHNG=3 means populations can increase by at most 3x
!   [CONSIS_CNT] Check adjacent population consistency every N iterations
!                (0 or absent = no check; still under development)
!
! Default: all parameters at their CMFGEN defaults
!          (RELAX=1.0, T_LIM=0.2, MAX_CHNG=100*CHANGE_LIM)
!
! prepare_VADAT.py overwrites this file when adjust_corrections
! is specified in the YAML config.
!
1 [L_ST]
394 [L_END]
1.0D0 [RELAX]
0.2D0 [T_LIM]
1.0D3 [MAX_CHNG]
0 [CONSIS_CNT]
